/**
\page specsep_lane iccSpecSepToTiff: spectral separation TIFF lane

\tableofcontents

\section specsep_cli Positional arguments after option removal

`iccSpecSepToTiff` combines numbered, single-channel grayscale TIFF inputs
into one multi-sample TIFF. The parser first removes recognized options from
any position in `argv`: `--ifd N`, `--tiles WIDTH HEIGHT`, `--bigtiff`, and,
when telemetry is compiled in, the telemetry/file options. It then rebuilds
`argv` from the remaining positional tokens. The reduced `argc` must be 8
(program plus seven fields) or 9 (with an optional profile):

| Reduced token | Name | Contract |
|---|---|---|
| `argv[0]` | program | Invocation name |
| `argv[1]` | output | Destination TIFF path |
| `argv[2]` | compress | Literal `0` (none) or `1` (LZW) |
| `argv[3]` | sep | Literal `0` (interleaved) or `1` (separate) |
| `argv[4]` | infile_prefix | Literal prefix; channel number is appended |
| `argv[5]`, `[6]`, `[7]` | start, end, incr | Signed decimal range; nonzero step must land exactly on end |
| `argv[8]` | profile | Optional conformant, sample-matching ICC profile |

`--ifd N` selects the same zero-based main-chain IFD, 0 through 4095, from
every input; the default is 0. Other main IFDs and selected-directory SubIFDs
are reported but not copied. `--tiles` requires positive dimensions divisible
by 16. `--bigtiff` selects BigTIFF rather than the classic TIFF default.
Duplicate, malformed, or unknown `--` options and an unavailable selected IFD
fail before output creation. Mixed help/version requests are rejected; the
literal prefix is not a `printf` pattern.

\dotfile specsep-lane.dot "iccSpecSepToTiff option parsing and image assembly"

\section specsep_help Help, output, and receipts

`-h`, `--help`, and `--version` succeed only as standalone invocations.
Malformed or incomplete conversions print diagnostics to stderr. Mixed
help/version requests and unknown long options fail with status 1. Most older
conversion failure paths return `-1` (exit 255 on POSIX); graceful exit-code
normalization is tracked in the \ref md_docs_2analysis_2image-tool-tiff-qa-2026-11-01
"image-tool audit".

For each input in turn, its main chain is inventoried without pixel decoding,
then its selected IFD is opened for pixels. Dimensions, resolution, sample encoding,
and photometric layout must match. The optional profile is checked before
output creation. The tool writes one output IFD, with optional tiled and
BigTIFF layout. Telemetry-enabled builds report selected IFD provenance,
aggregate main-IFD counts, ignored SubIFD references, and read/write work.

See \ref tiff_processing_pipeline "TIFF image processing pipeline" for the
cross-tool view and `Tools/CmdLine/IccSpecSepToTiff/Readme.md` for limits and
examples.
*/
